====================================================================================================
Q(0) for the odd numbers is exact
====================================================================================================
  N_d = d, L_d = d^2, s_d = d(2d-1)(2d+1)/3, delta_d = d + d^2/2
  sum_{d>=1} 2^-d (delta_d^2 - s_d/4) = 61   exactly
  Gamma(odds) = 3, so Q(0) = 61/3 = 20.3333333333
  and the relative error of the annealed prediction at the centre is
  Q(0)/sigma^2 with sigma^2 = k(4k^2-1)/12, i.e. asymptotically 61/k^3.
